# Security headers for hosts that read Netlify's `_headers` format.
#
# This file exists because the same site is deployed to more than one host and
# each reads a different configuration file. Vercel reads `vercel.json`,
# Netlify reads this file, and Render reads the `headers:` block in
# `render.yaml`. A header added to only one of them protects only one
# deployment - and which host serves the production domain is not something the
# code can know.
#
# Vite copies everything in `public/` into `dist/` verbatim, so this lands at
# the publish root where Netlify looks for it. Hosts that do not use this
# format ignore it, which is why it is safe to ship everywhere.
#
# KEEP THE THREE IN SYNC. If you change a directive here, change it in
# `vercel.json` and `render.yaml` too. The CSP in particular is derived from
# what the app actually loads - see docs/SECURITY_AUDIT.md for what each
# directive is for, and re-verify in a browser after changing it, because a
# wrong CSP is a white screen.
#
# img-src lists the only image origins the app uses: its own /images, data:
# upload previews, and uploaded /uploads/ files on the API host.
# style-src has no 'unsafe-inline' because nothing injects <style> elements.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://iunu-api.onrender.com; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://iunu-api.onrender.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
